  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which builds the whole handcart procedurally. It passes the typecheck, but I couldn't run it, so the rendering is unchecked. I haven't run `vite build` either.\n\n- **Bed:** 8 floor planks, 4 side boards and 2 end boards, so `plankCount` is 14. The planks vary in length, thickness, tilt and tone. Each corner has a post with 2 cross rails on every side. There are iron straps and bolts on the sides and under the floor.\n- **Wheels:** 2 wheels, each with a hub, 2 iron bands, 10 spokes, 10 wooden rim segments and iron tyre segments. They sit on a shared axle with iron linchpins. Both turn slowly in place.\n- **Chassis:** 2 long rear push handles tilt slightly upward at the back. A front prop stand has two legs and a cross brace.\n- **Load:** 2 barrels with iron hoops, 4 sacks in the bed, and 3 crates, two of them stacked. One sack and one barrel stand on the ground by the prop leg.\n- **Scene:** The cart stands on a dirt ground with patches and 22 scattered stones that stay clear of the cart. A warm directional sun casts soft shadows, with a warm hemisphere light and fog. The orbit camera starts at a three-quarter view and turns slowly (about 25 seconds per revolution).\n- **Flags:** After the first frame it sets `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` and `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { ready: true, wheelCount: 2, spokeCount: 20, plankCount: 14 }`.\n\nI set the shadow options (map size, filter, softness, bias) from the type definitions. How soft and how stable the shadows look is untested.\n\n",
